A few months ago, after setting my ethernet settings by hand rather than
relying on autonegotiation, my disk errors went away.  Now they are 
back.  I have a slowly increasing error count (1 more count per day or 
so) on one physical member of a shadow set (no errors on the virtual 
unit).  Moreover, these errors are visible from only one node in the 
cluster, which is also the only node to which the "bad" member has a 
direct connection.  There are no other errors which are increasing and 
only a few altogether (most of them occur during boot, IIRC a known 
problem with the hardware models I have).

Is this enough information to determine if the error is due to the disk 
itself, or could it be a problem with the controller, cable etc?

I could swap the disk and, after a full copy, see if the problem goes 
away, but it would be nice to be able to get some more information 
first.



